{
  "user_message": "is AI dangerous?",
  "chatbot_response": "While AI itself isn't inherently \"dangerous,\" it does come with significant environmental costs. The energy consumption of large language models like myself is roughly 10 times higher than a typical Google search, which can lead to substantial CO2 emissions. To put this into perspective, the training of a single model like GPT-4 emitted around 500 tonnes of CO2, equivalent to about 100,000 flights from New York to Los Angeles.",
  "agent_state": "educator",
