{
  "user_message": "how much co2 is released per query in chatgpt",
  "chatbot_response": "Unfortunately, the exact amount of CO2 released per query in ChatGPT isn't publicly disclosed, but we can estimate it based on the overall energy consumption of LLMs. Given that LLMs use roughly 10 times more energy than a Google search, and a typical Google search emits around 0.2 grams of CO2, we can estimate that a single query in ChatGPT might emit around 2 grams of CO2. To put this into perspective, this is equivalent to the CO2 emissions from driving a car for about 1-2 kilometers.",
